  "id": "osf-symlink-resolution",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-07T10:09:37.124Z",
  "title": "Symlink resolution in osf check and scan",
  "summary": "Adds a shared `symlink` module that decides what a symlink means to the scanner. Previously every symlink was skipped and counted as excluded; now a link whose real target lives inside the repository is followed to the real files behind it, while a link pointing outside the repository, into `.git`, at nothing, or in a loop is refused with a `symlink refused:` error. `check scan`, `check lint-writing` and `check lint-skill` expand their path arguments through the new module before existence checks and scanning, and the directory walker in `scan` now resolves links instead of counting them.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
